  "content": {
    "id": "p5-q16-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "16",
    "prompt": "",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p5-q16-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Simplify $(k+1)^3-k^3$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3k^2+3k+1$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(k+1)^3-k^3&=k^3+3k^2+3k+1-k^3\\\\(k+1)^3-k^3&=3k^2+3k+1.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p5-q16-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, find a formula for the sum\n$$1^2+2^2+\\cdots+n^2.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\displaystyle\\frac{n(n+1)(2n+1)}{6}$.\n\nSum the differences from part (a); the cubes telescope.",
          "worked": "Let $S=1^2+2^2+\\cdots+n^2$. Sum part (a) for $k=1,2,\\ldots,n$. The cube differences telescope, and $1+2+\\cdots+n=\\frac{n(n+1)}2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(n+1)^3-1&=3S+3\\frac{n(n+1)}2+n\\\\3S&=(n+1)^3-1-\\frac{3n(n+1)}2-n\\\\3S&=n^3+\\frac32n^2+\\frac12n\\\\3S&=\\frac{n(n+1)(2n+1)}2\\\\S&=\\frac{n(n+1)(2n+1)}6.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 66
      }
    ]
  },
